  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There is a set of NNN cards where each card is numbered 111 to NNN.\n\nChef throws a card numbered XXX.\n\nFind the number of ways, Chefina can chose a card from the remaining deck such that, the sum of chosen card and XXX is **even**.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two space-separated integers NNN and XXX — the number of cards and the card thrown by Chef.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the number of ways, Chefina can chose a card from the remaining deck such that, the sum of chosen card and XXX is **even**.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤10002 \\leq N \\leq 10002≤N≤1000",
      "1≤X≤N1 \\leq X \\leq N1≤X≤N"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3 1\n2 2\n5 4",
        "output": "1\n0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Chefina can only chose card numbered 333 such that the sum is 3+1=43+1=43+1=4, which is even.\nTest case 222: There are two cards and Chef throws card numbered 222. Thus, Chefina cannot chose any card such that sum is even.\nTest case 333: Chefina can only chose card numbered 222 such that the sum is 4+2=64+2=64+2=6, which is even."
      }
    ]
  },
